From d5b339895370dbbab5997c81e3459dcaccdce073 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Santiago Postacchini <postacchinisantiago@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:32:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Teclado: el marcador (KEYCATCH_SCORES) no suelta las teclas
 apretadas

Al abrirse con Tab, cgame levanta KEYCATCH_SCORES; Key_SetCatcher llamaba a
Key_ClearStates, que mandaba -scores y cerraba el marcador con Tab mantenido.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 code/client/cl_keys.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/code/client/cl_keys.c b/code/client/cl_keys.c
index ea9beaa..be22912 100644
--- a/code/client/cl_keys.c
+++ b/code/client/cl_keys.c
@@ -1385,8 +1385,10 @@ Key_SetCatcher
 ====================
 */
 void Key_SetCatcher(int catcher) {
-    // If the catcher state is changing, clear all key states
-    if (catcher != keyCatchers)
+    // If the catcher state is changing, clear all key states.
+    // QuakeWeb: el bit KEYCATCH_SCORES no cuenta. cgame lo levanta en el frame siguiente a "+scores" (marcador
+    // visible); si eso soltaba las teclas, el Tab mantenido recibía su "-scores" y el marcador se cerraba solo.
+    if ((catcher & ~KEYCATCH_SCORES) != (keyCatchers & ~KEYCATCH_SCORES))
         Key_ClearStates();
 
     keyCatchers = catcher;
-- 
